<!-- Worked example: a typical verdict-1.7 record.

     1.7 names the decision behind the verdict (Statistical Companion
     1.5.0). The record states the methodology whose rules produced it, and
     the verdict states the versioned rule that decided.

     The run below is an empirical regression test: a baseline of 951
     successes in 1000 trials, a test of 100 samples, alpha 0.05. Under
     regression/fisher (the one-sided Fisher exact test) the baseline and
     the test are weighed jointly, and the integer cutoff is c = 91: the
     test PASSes iff at least 91 of its 100 samples succeed. It observed 93, so it passes. The stated
     threshold is c / n_t = 0.91, the rate the cutoff corresponds to; the
     Wilson lower bound is descriptive and decides nothing.

     A configuration refused before any sample ran is shown in
     verdict-1.7-refused.xml. -->
